 "renames": {},
 "notes": [
  "M7 part b: the 151 content files NLAlib/Matrix/[I-Q]*.lean merged from main (#21, #24); NLAlib/Matrix/{Inequalities,Norms,OperatorTheory,Perturbation}.lean are generated aggregators and are not mapped. No renames: no base name collides with a file already in its destination leaf.",
  "All 151 files import only Mathlib, NLAlib.ForMathlib.* and NLAlib.Matrix.*; none has a Probability/measure-theory import, so all stay in layer 0.",
  "Families kept together, one leaf each: Interlacing* (+ LowRankInterlacing) -> Spectral; Normal*, MatrixPower* (+ PowerBoundedOrbits), Ordered*/PrimaryTriangularization/Quasi* (Schur triangularisation and real quasitriangular / pencil forms) -> Spectral; Majorization*, KyFan*, Lidskii*/Mirsky*, Kantorovich family (Kantorovich, PositiveSpectralEndpoints, QuadraticConditionBounds), log-det family (LogDetConcavity, MinkowskiDeterminant), Hadamard-Fischer principal-minor family (InverseDiagonalMinor, PrincipalMinorProducts, PrincipalMinorProductBounds, PrincipalOverlapDeterminant, OverlappingBlockDeterminant) -> Inequalities; InvariantNorm*, Nuclear* -> Norms; LeastSquares* (atlas least-squares-perturbation), Pseudoinverse* (atlas pseudoinverse-perturbation), InversePerturbationBounds, LinearSystemPerturbation, MapConditioning, PopulationTraceGap -> Perturbation; PrincipalAngle* (+ InverseOverlapGram), Oblique*, Projection*/ProjectorBlocks, Orthogonal* -> Subspaces; LU*, QR*, MaximumVolume* (strong RRQR), Polar*/NearestPolar, Procrustes* -> Factorizations; Kronecker* -> Structured; LoewnerHeinz -> OperatorTheory; Jacobi*, MoorePenrose*, PSD-cone facts (PSDDuality, PositiveDefiniteClosure, PositiveSemidefiniteSeries) -> Basic.",
  "Pseudoinverse* goes to Perturbation, not Basic/Factorizations as the file-name hint suggests: every file of the family is part of the pseudoinverse-perturbation (Wedin / Stewart-Sun III.3) development, including the exact identities PseudoinverseDifference/PseudoinverseProjectors that exist only to feed it. The same holds for LeastSquaresGeometry/LeastSquaresEuclidean within the LeastSquares* perturbation family.",
  "Cross-leaf imports created (all within Matrix, layer 0, no file-level cycle): Norms<->Inequalities (InvariantNorm/Nuclear* import KyFan*; KyFanNormToolkit imports Nuclear*), Subspaces<->Factorizations (OrthogonalSumCompletion imports QRCompletion; MaximumVolumeQR imports OrthogonalSumCompletion)."
 ],
 "flags": [
  "NLAlib/Matrix/KyFanNorms.lean, KyFanFiniteIndex.lean, KyFanNormToolkit.lean: these define and axiomatise the Ky Fan norms (atlas ky-fan-norms-def) and would read naturally in Norms; kept with the KyFan* family in Inequalities because KyFanNorms sits in the middle of the KyFan import chain (KyFan -> KyFanAttainment -> KyFanNorms -> KyFanFiniteIndex -> KyFanTrace/KyFanSums). Revisit if the family is split by atlas tag (ky-fan-maximum-principle vs ky-fan-norms-def).",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/NuclearHermitian.lean: nuclear norm = sum of |eigenvalues| plus a Lidskii-based nuclear variation bound (atlas lidskii); placed with Nuclear* in Norms, could equally go to Inequalities with Lidskii.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/PlaneRotation*.lean (4 files): plane-rotation tools that exist only for the Schur-Horn variational proof (imported by SchurHorn, SchurHornDescent); placed in Inequalities on the assumption that part c places SchurHorn* in Inequalities (majorization). If SchurHorn* goes to Spectral, move PlaneRotation* with it.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/IrreducibleDiagonalDominance.lean: Taussky's theorem, imports GershgorinBasic; placed in Spectral assuming Gershgorin* goes to Spectral (part a). Move with Gershgorin* if it lands in Perturbation.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/ProductWeyl.lean, ProductSingularValues.lean: multiplicative singular-value inequalities (Weyl, Horn); placed in Spectral next to Spectral/Weyl.lean; Inequalities is an equally defensible home (ProductSingularValues imports KyFan).",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/Procrustes*.lean, NearestPolar.lean: approximation-by-isometries results built on PolarDecomposition; placed with Polar* in Factorizations (ScaledOrthogonal, imported by ProcrustesToolkit, belongs in the same leaf; part c should match).",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/MaximumVolume*.lean: maximum-volume column selection / strong RRQR blocks; placed in Factorizations, where StrongRankRevealingQR and RankRevealingLeading (part c) should also go.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/PrincipalMinorPSD.lean: Sylvester's criterion (principal minors / charpoly coefficients characterise PSD); placed in Spectral next to Spectral/PrincipalMinors.lean which it imports.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/Kronecker*.lean: Kronecker product identities, spectra, singular values; placed in Structured (structured matrices). Spectral would also fit for KroneckerSpectrum/KroneckerSingularValues; kept as one family.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/QuasiTriangular.lean, QuasiPencilBasis.lean: real quasitriangular pattern and orthogonal pencil reduction (real Schur / generalized Schur); placed with the Schur family in Spectral; Factorizations would also fit.",
  "NLAlib/Matrix/IndefiniteCongruence.lean: simultaneous diagonalisation by congruence for an invertible indefinite form; placed in Spectral with the Simultaneous* family it imports."
 ]
}